│  Highlights\n\n- Largest regional market: Asia Pacific (41.7% revenue       │
│  share, 2025)\n\n### Market Size & Forecast\n\n- Market size in 2025: USD   │
│  82.4 Billion\n- Estimated market size in 2026: USD 86.3 Billion\n-         │
│  Projected market size by 2033: USD 136.9 Billion\n- CAGR (2026-2033):      │
│  6.8%\n\nMoreover, the rise of [smart                                       │
│  buildings](https://www.grandviewresearch.com/industry-analysis/global-sma  │
│  rt-buildings-market), which incorporate IoT and energy-efficient           │
│  technologies, is further propelling the market. Modern elevators cater to  │
│  a wide range of uses, including the movement of goods, people, as well as  │
│  in ships, dams, and specialist structures like rocket launchers.           │
│  Furthermore, in the coming years, demand for elevators will be driven by   │
│  the development of collective operation, in which an elevator or group of  │
│  elevators offers enhanced automatic operation and is popular in            │
│  residential complexes and hospitals due to its affordability. One such     │
│  company is Toshiba Johnson Elevators India (TJEI), which improves lives    │
│  through technology and design.\n\n![Elevators market size and growth       │
│  forecast                                                                   │
│  (2023-2033)](https://www.grandviewresearch.com/static/img/research/elevat  │
│  ors-market-size.webp)\n\nAdditionally, TJEI offers an extensive product    │
│  offering of ultra-premium and premium-class elevators. SPACEL-III and      │
│  High-end ELCOSMO-III are two products in this segment. The ELBRIGHT        │
│  series of these elevators uses a small traction machine to save time and   │
│  energy while cutting the machine room's size by up to 50%. These           │
│  aforementioned factors will drive the demand for elevators in the coming   │
│  years.\n\n## Market Dynamics\n\nThe elevators market is shaped by          │
│  accelerating urbanization, increasing high-rise construction activity,     │
│  and growing investments in residential, commercial, institutional, and     │
│  transportation infrastructure. Rising demand for efficient, safe, and      │
│  reliable vertical mobility solutions across smart buildings, mixed-use     │
│  developments, airports, healthcare facilities, and transit hubs continues  │
│  to support market growth. Technological advancements, including            │
│  IoT-enabled monitoring, predictive maintenance, destination control        │
│  systems, touchless interfaces, and energy-efficient elevator               │
│  technologies, are further enhancing operational efficiency and user        │
│  experience. However, high installation, maintenance, and modernization     │
│  costs, coupled with stringent safety standards and regulatory compliance   │
│  requirements, may constrain adoption in certain markets. Despite these     │
│  challenges, significant growth opportunities are emerging from the         │
│  modernization of aging elevator infrastructure, increasing penetration of  │
│  smart building ecosystems, and rising demand for sustainable solutions     │
│  such as machine-room-less elevators, regenerative drive systems, and       │
│  digitally connected elevator platforms.\n\n### [Drivers - Rising Urban     │
│  Development and Vertical Construction Supporting Market                    │
│  Growth](https://www.grandviewresearch.com/industry-analysis/elevators-mar  │
│  ket-report\\#collapseOne)\n\nRapid urbanization, increasing population     │
│  density, and limited land availability in major cities are accelerating    │
│  the construction of high-rise residential and commercial buildings,        │
│  thereby driving demand for elevators. Governments and private developers   │
│  continue to invest in smart cities, mixed-use developments, healthcare     │
│  facilities, airports, metro stations, and commercial complexes, further    │
│  supporting market expansion. The growing need for efficient vertical       │
│  transportation systems that enhance accessibility, convenience, and        │
│  building efficiency is also contributing to demand. In addition, rising    │
│  investments in affordable housing and urban infrastructure projects        │
│  across emerging economies are creating long-term growth opportunities for  │
│  elevator manufacturers and service providers.\n\n### [Restraint -          │
│  Elevated Ownership Costs and Regulatory Challenges Limiting                │
│  Adoption](https://www.grandviewresearch.com/industry-analysis/elevators-m  │
│  arket-report\\#collapseTwo)\n\nMarket growth is constrained by the         │
│  significant capital required for installation, modernization, and          │
│  lifecycle servicing of elevator systems. Compliance with evolving safety   │
│  regulations, certification standards, and inspection requirements adds to  │
│  operational complexity and overall ownership costs. In addition,           │
│  fluctuations in material prices, labor shortages, and the technical        │
│  expertise required for servicing sophisticated systems can increase        │
│  project expenses and affect profitability for stakeholders across the      │
│  value chain.\n\n### [Opportunity - Infrastructure Modernization and        │
│  Digitalization Creating New Revenue                                        │
│  Streams](https://www.grandviewresearch.com/industry-analysis/elevators-ma  │
│  rket-report\\#collapseThree)\n\nThe modernization and replacement of       │
│  aging elevator systems present significant growth opportunities,           │
│  particularly in developed regions with a large installed base of older     │
│  elevators. Building owners are increasingly investing in upgrades that     │
│  improve energy efficiency, passenger safety, and operational reliability   │
│  while extending equipment lifespan. The growing adoption of smart          │
│  elevators equipped with IoT connectivity, remote monitoring, [predictive   │
│  maintenance](https://www.grandviewresearch.com/industry-analysis/predicti  │
│  ve-maintenance-market), destination dispatch systems, and touchless        │
│  controls is creating new revenue streams for manufacturers and service     │
│  providers.\n\n### **Analyst Perspective**\n\n> The elevators market is     │
│  shaped by a combination of urbanization trends, construction activity,     │
│  infrastructure development, technological innovation, and building safety  │
│  requirements. Demand for vertical mobility solutions continues to be       │
│  driven by the expansion of high-rise residential and commercial            │
│  buildings, mixed-use developments, transportation hubs, healthcare         │
│  facilities, and public infrastructure projects. Building owners and        │
│  developers are increasingly prioritizing systems that enhance passenger    │
│  flow, energy efficiency, reliability, and user experience while            │
│  minimizing lifecycle costs. Technological advancements in smart controls,  │
│  predictive maintenance, destination dispatch systems, touchless            │
│  interfaces, and connected monitoring platforms are improving operational   │
│  efficiency and asset performance.\n\n## **Type Insights**\n\n> **“The      │
│  demand for the machine room-less traction type segment is expected to      │
│  grow at a significant CAGR of 7.5% from 2025 to 2030 in terms of           │
│  revenue.”**\n\nBased on type, the traction segment led the market with     │
│  the largest revenue share of 55.1% in 2025. Traction elevators are         │
│  frequently used in industrial and commercial structures. Additionally,     │
│  the expansion of infrastructure projects for commercial buildings,         │
│  including offices, malls, and retail centers, is expected to fuel the      │
│  market demand. Furthermore, the global market will have profitable growth  │
│  prospects due to favorable government measures supporting the building     │
│  sector.\n\nThe demand for machine room-less (MRL) traction elevators is    │
│  on the rise, driven by several factors. MRL elevators offer space-saving   │
│  benefits, as they eliminate the need for a separate machine room,          │
│  allowing for more usable building space and flexibility in design. This    │
│  is particularly appealing in urban environments where maximizing floor     │
│  area is crucial. Additionally, MRL elevators are often more                │
│  energy-efficient, contributing to lower operational costs and reduced      │
│  environmental impact, which aligns with the growing emphasis on            │
│  sustainability in construction.\n\n## **Business Insights**\n\n> **“The    │
│  demand for the maintenance business segment is expected to grow at a       │
│  significant CAGR of 7.4% from 2025 to 2030 in terms of                     │
│  revenue.”**\n\nBased on business, the new equipment segment led the        │
│  market with the largest revenue share of 47.6% in 2025. The demand for     │
│  elevators in the new equipment type business is gaining momentum, largely  │
│  driven by the rapid expansion of urban infrastructure and the increasing   │
│  complexity of modern buildings. As developers seek innovative solutions    │
│  to enhance building functionality, elevators are evolving into             │
│  sophisticated systems that integrate smart technology, energy efficiency,  │
│  and improved safety features.\n\nRising technological developments aimed   │
│  at raising maintenance standards for elevators at different low-rise       │
│  construction sites have been a significant factor in the market's          │
